  "notes": "{緩|ゆる}む means for something tight or tense to become loose or relaxed, either physically or figuratively.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {緩|ゆる}める (transitive — to loosen something)\n- Pattern: Xが{緩|ゆる}む\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{緩|ゆる}んでいる indicates a current state of being loose: ねじが{緩|ゆる}んでいる (the screw is loose).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ねじが{緩|ゆる}む: a screw becomes loose\n- {気|き}が{緩|ゆる}む: to let one's guard down\n- {規制|きせい}が{緩|ゆる}む: regulations are relaxed\n- {表情|ひょうじょう}が{緩|ゆる}む: one's expression softens\n- {寒|さむ}さが{緩|ゆる}む: the cold eases up\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {緩|ゆる}める: to loosen (transitive)\n- {緩|ゆる}い: loose, slack, lax (adjective)",
